1. e4 c5 2. Nf3 d6 3. d4 cxd4 4. Nxd4 Nf6 5. Nc3 a6 6. Bc4 e6 7. a3 Be7 8. Ba2 O-O 9. O-O b5 10. f4 Bb7 11. f5 e5 12. Nde2 Nxe4 $2 {This is a crucial mistake. White gains important tempi to attack.} 13. Nxe4 Bxe4 14. Ng3 Bc6 {Preferred to Bb7, in order to defend the N (after it comes to d7) from the expected Qg4, releasing the BQ to manoeuvre.} 15. f6 $5 {White['s plan] becomes clear. Brutal threats are to be expected. (Nicolai)} Bxf6 16. Nh5 Nd7 17. Qg4 Qb6+ 18. Kh1 Qd4 19. Qg3 Kh8 ({Stockfish 17:} 19... Be4 $17) 20. Bg5 Bxg5 21. Qxg5 g6 22. c3 f6 ({Stockfish 17:} 22... Qb6 $15) 23. Nxf6 (23. Qh6 $2 Bxg2+ 24. Kxg2 Qe4+ 25. Kh3 gxh5 $19) 23... Qd3 24. Kg1 Nxf6 25. Rxf6 Bd5 $3 $11 26. Raf1 (26. Rxd6 $4 Qe2 $1 $19) 26... Rxf6 27. Qxf6+ Kg8 28. Bxd5+ Qxd5 29. h4 $2 ({The first serious mistake in this game, which was otherwise played admirably by White} 29. Qe7 $1 {and Black can hardly do anything. He would have to play} e4 {where White has at least a draw. Now Black frees himself from his grasp (Nicolai)}) 29... Re8 $1 30. h5 Qe6 31. hxg6 hxg6 32. Qg5 Kg7 33. Rf3 Qe7 34. Qxe7+ Rxe7 35. Rd3 Rd7 36. a4 d5 37. axb5 axb5 38. Kf2 Rd6 39. Rd1 Kf6 40. Ra1 b4 41. Ke3 bxc3 42. bxc3 Rc6 43. Kd3 (43. Ra3 $2 Rxc3+ $1) 43... Kf5 44. Ra5 Rd6 45. Ra4 e4+ 46. Kd4 Kf4 47. Ra2 e3 48. Re2 Re6 49. Kxd5 Re8 50. c4 Rd8+ 51. Ke6 Rd2 52. Re1 Rxg2 53. Rc1 Rd2 54. c5 e2 55. c6 Rd1 56. Rc4+ Kf3 57. Rc3+ Kf2 58. Rc2 Kf1 {Source: Schach Echo, 1968/4} 0-1

