1. d4 Nf6 2. c4 g6 3. Nc3 d5 4. cxd5 Nxd5 5. e4 Nxc3 6. bxc3 c5 7. Bc4 cxd4 8. cxd4 Qb6 9. Qd3 Bg7 10. Ne2 Nc6 11. Rb1 Qd8 12. Be3 O-O (12... Na5) 13. a3 Kh8 ({The king's attack planned with this is premature before the queenside has developed.} 13... Na5 {or 13...b6 were also appropriate here.}) 14. O-O f5 15. Bd5 e5 {Too stormy.} 16. dxe5 Nxe5 17. Qb3 Qh4 18. f3 f4 19. Bd4 g5 {('d5' is given in the text. The note given by Cherubim, translated by Google, reads: "Black doesn't think about the danger that threatens him and blocks his queen from the action on the main theatre of war." which seems to indicate that ...g5 was played. JS)} 20. Qc3 Re8 21. Bxb7 Rb8 22. Bc6 Rxb1 23. Rxb1 Re7 24. Rb8 Nxf3+ 25. gxf3 Qh3 26. Bxg7+ Rxg7 27. Bd5 {Source: Schach Echo, 1968/2} 1-0

